{
  "requirement": "The SDK supplies the inspection tools described in\n[Validation context](validation-context.md). Graph tools invoke the application's graph\nand contents interfaces; source tools invoke its source interfaces and\nsource-node mapping.\n\nThe SDK provides a fixed set of tools and their input-recording policy.\nApplication-specific node kinds use the SDK's ordinary node-read tool.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "No gaps found. Each obligation of `fixed_tools` maps to a marked test with assertions.\n\n**Fixed tool set.**\n- `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` (`configured.rs`) checks the exact ordered tool names sent on the wire when no sources are attached: `read_node`, `outgoing_edges`, `get_next_page`, `submit_result`.\n- `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` (`tests.rs`) checks the same list at the provider-request level. It also checks the `get_next_page` schema.\n- `configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions` (`configured.rs`) checks the exact list with sources attached. It adds `list_sources`, `outline_source`, `search_text`, `search_structure` and `finish_search`. It also checks that the `node` parameter of `read_node`, `outline_source` and `outgoing_edges` is an integer-id reference.\n\n**Graph tools invoke the graph and contents interfaces.**\n- `graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery` exercises `outgoing_edges`, `read_node` and `get_next_page` against a graph. It asserts the recorded edge and node-content observations.\n- It also covers the policy for undelivered results. A failed delivery records nothing, and a queued-contents delivery records its node.\n- `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` asserts that the graph's `outgoing_edges` is called exactly once. It also asserts the delivered target list and the recorded `OutgoingEdges` dependency. Malformed node IDs are rejected before any graph query. A failed delivery adds no input. A second label is recorded separately.\n- `queued_contents_and_graph_read_tools_redact_credentials_before_delivery` checks that node contents are delivered from the graph's contents and that the recorded fingerprint is of the original.\n\n**Source tools invoke the source interfaces and the source-node mapping.**\n- `source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results` drives `list_sources`, `search_text`, `search_structure`, `outline_source` and `read_source` against a recording provider. It asserts the exact arguments the provider receives, namely prefix, context and limit. It asserts the delivered shapes. It asserts that discovery records no dependencies and that reads record the mapped observation. It also asserts that provider errors surface.\n- `configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions` runs end to end over the local transport. It uses `list_sources` and `read_node` on a source-mapped id. It asserts the delivered text is the mapped snapshot and not the disk contents. It exercises `search_text` and `finish_search`. It asserts the exact dependency list, which has the source-mapped nodes carrying outline fingerprints. It asserts that only the selected file was read, once per execution.\n- `structural_tags_select_only_the_original_enclosing_item` and `outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items` (`project_sources.rs`) cover `search_structure`, `finish_search`, `outline_source` and `get_next_page`, including paging and which calls record dependencies.\n\n**Input-recording policy.** Discovery calls (list, search, outline, pages) record nothing. Reads and finished searches record node observations. These asserts appear across the tests above.\n\n**Application-specific node kinds use the ordinary node-read tool.** Domain node ids, including source-mapped ids, are read only through `read_node`. The tool list has no kind-specific read tool, and the tests read mapped source nodes through `read_node`.\n\nThe more detailed per-tool behavior, MCP schemas and input rules are covered by the refining requirements (`read_node.*`, `outgoing_edges.*`, `list_sources.*`, `pages.*` and others) and their own tests. They are not reassessed here. The umbrella obligation is covered, and no fixme acknowledgments exist or are needed.",
  "references": "f4ee5d1041aba8580bbb03e3ce8a5f36e34ff867cd73b2cc4a9cb8f305ed639f",
